{"id": "EUVD-2026-76303", "enisaUuid": "86d945ca-7ea0-31aa-90dd-89b764725a5c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: stop killed, freed and out_of_sync sharing a byte\n\nThe three connection state flags are single-bit bitfields, so they occupy\none byte of struct smc_connection and every store to one is a\nread-modify-write of the other two:\n\n    u8  killed : 1;\n    u8  freed : 1;\n    u8  out_of_sync : 1;\n\nThey are not written under a common lock. smc_cdc_msg_validate() sets\nout_of_sync from the receive tasklet, while smc_conn_kill() sets killed\nfrom process context under lock_sock(), and the receive path does not defer\nto the backlog when the socket is owned -- smc_cdc_msg_recv() takes only\nbh_lock_sock().\n\nGive each flag its own byte so a store no longer touches its neighbours.\nAll readers test them as booleans and are unchanged. struct smc_connection\ngrows by two bytes.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:21", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/297e96f38d3e4f1a3b84068950dd5c7a55bbdc7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09a9cbadc05f452405de31012bd2c428b601291a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/313f79149eb337411c64e2c247234b62ef9a3cb9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2cb7a8d64b7e8ccdc69bbe48fe9c4eaa79c33aec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db51a8658c11a82432b64999519a269c3aabb447"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80980", "GHSA-74wv-6pxv-7x55"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3ef3dd9c-18c5-38c4-94cd-9ffdb54a1282", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b286a0651e4404ab96cdfdcdad8a839a26b3751e <db51a8658c11a82432b64999519a269c3aabb447"}, {"id": "59020ca3-0ac2-34b5-bf26-dbb86a9c32bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "5bd29e22-ca79-3289-a642-8cab410faba3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "7a0f4964-1193-32c3-8128-77700fce0114", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b286a0651e4404ab96cdfdcdad8a839a26b3751e <09a9cbadc05f452405de31012bd2c428b601291a"}, {"id": "8cf8230e-a727-3c15-beb0-387890286a25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "937db69a-1fe2-305b-981e-aee54f2f45e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9b0716ad-3a93-3d93-97a4-9a9bf93426e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b286a0651e4404ab96cdfdcdad8a839a26b3751e <297e96f38d3e4f1a3b84068950dd5c7a55bbdc7b"}, {"id": "c11ad3d4-242d-382f-a73f-a01011311b0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b286a0651e4404ab96cdfdcdad8a839a26b3751e <313f79149eb337411c64e2c247234b62ef9a3cb9"}, {"id": "d38fb648-630d-39ad-96e1-6b5c99e07e29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d3d01467-41c8-34fa-af84-f2b6c26dccd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "f7a37d27-4c45-320e-b011-796b6852099a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b286a0651e4404ab96cdfdcdad8a839a26b3751e <2cb7a8d64b7e8ccdc69bbe48fe9c4eaa79c33aec"}, {"id": "fae94c7a-9639-3598-8d94-390d129c0046", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e9945b9d-b662-3406-8585-cbdb3ae4c6ae", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}